  "question": {
    "text": "A magnetic dipole experiences a torque of $80 \\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{~N} \\mathrm{~m}$ when placed in uniform magnetic field in such a way that dipole moment makes angle of $60^{\\circ}$ with magnetic field. The potential energy of the dipole is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$80 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-40 \\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-60 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-80 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\tau=\\mathrm{M} \\times \\mathrm{B}=\\mathrm{MB} \\sin 60=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\mathrm{MB}=80 \\sqrt{3}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{MB}=160 \\\\ & \\mathrm{U}=-\\mathrm{M} \\cdot \\mathrm{B}=-\\mathrm{MB} \\cos 60 \\\\ & \\mathrm{U}=-160 \\times 1 / 2=-80 \\mathrm{~J}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}